{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":754,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"Dynamic programming counting binary strings of length 13 avoiding 000 and 111\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 13 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 same bits. Classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run length 2. For each bit type? Actually we can treat symmetrical. Let A_n be sequences length n ending with a single bit (i.e., last two bits different or n=1). B_n ending with two identical bits (run length 2). Recurrence: For next bit, if we add different bit, run length becomes 1. If we add same bit, we can only if previous run length 1 (since can't go to 3). So:\n\nA_{n+1} = A_n + B_n (adding different bit to any sequence). B_{n+1} = A_n (adding same bit to sequences ending with run length 1). Base n=1: sequences \"0\" and \"1\": both run length 1. So A_1=2, B_1=0.\n\nCompute up to n=13.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=2 B=0 total=2\nn=2: A2 = A1+B1 =2+0=2; B2 = A1=2; total=4\nn=3: A3 = A2+B2 =2+2=4; B3 = A2=2; total=6\nn=4: A4 = A3+B3 =4+2=6; B4 = A3=4; total=10\nn=5: A5 = A4+B4 =6+4=10; B5 = A4=6; total=16\nn=6: A6 = A5+B5 =10+6=16; B6 = A5=10; total=26\nn=7: A7 = A6+B6 =16+10=26; B7 = A6=16; total=42\nn=8: A8 = A7+B7 =26+16=42; B8 = A7=26; total=68\nn=9: A9 = A8+B8 =42+26=68; B9 = A8=42; total=110\nn=10: A10 = A9+B9 =68+42=110; B10 = A9=68; total=178\nn=11: A11 = A10+B10 =110+68=178; B11 = A10=110; total=288\nn=12: A12 = A11+B11 =178+110=288; B12 = A11=178; total=466\nn=13: A13 = A12+B12 =288+178=466; B13 = A12=288; total=754\n\nThus answer 754."}}],"created":1790946471,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outpu